  "slug": "association-adjusting-2e22",
  "summary": "Recent preprints and a PLOS CB paper extend kernel, mediation and latent-factor inference to combine evidence types or model dependence in association testing.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is association inference that pools heterogeneous evidence or explicitly models dependence rather than testing marginal single-variant effects. PrediXSKAT embeds PrediXcan-predicted expression in the SKAT kernel so rare coding and common cis-regulatory variants are tested jointly for gene-level power. GiMat extends multivariate kernel regression to SNP gene-gene interactions across multiple dichotomous phenotypes. QT-RelCor offers parametric and non-parametric tests linking quantitative traits to binary disease status in clustered family data. CAS-X integrates fine-mapped eQTL PIPs with allelic fold changes across five metabolic tissues to prioritize candidate effector genes at type 2 diabetes loci. Beyond genotype data, LaMe estimates natural direct and indirect effects via joint linear-Gaussian latent mediation in high-dimensional systems, and multiCAsp applies a graph-Laplacian spatial prior to canonical association across spatial multi-omics. Evidence is mostly preprint-stage; only GiMat is published.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-opus-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-20"
}
